/* CFGCMDBUFFERVALID @Bits 16..31 : Number of valid DWORDS (32 bits) in command buffer. FW updates this field to synchronize
                                    with HW and let HW progress upto this location. Each Entry is atleast 64 bitss. Entry[15:0]
                                    = address. Entry[19:16] = active low write byte enable, 0 = write all 4 bytes, E=write only
                                    first byte. Entry[31:24] = number of data DWORDS. Entry[63:32] = data0, .... Little endian
                                    format, ie Entry[31:0] is lower address than Entry[63:32] */

