/* CFGCMD @Bits 0..5 : currently it is 5bits [4:0], specify a required operation to be executed. In the notation used below,
                       capital letters (O,X,Y) represent vectors while small letters (o,a,b) represent scalars. When the output
                       is a vector (O) it is written to memory, when the output is scallar (o) is is available in the
                       accumulator status register (which can optionally be written to memory by setting cfg_write_acc in
                       descriptor.) */

