                                                                            /*!< Bit mask of ITEMS field.*/

/* TRANSFERS @Bits 16..23 : When TRANSFERSMODE=0: The number of DMA transfers in the DMA job, represented in 'natural' format
                            (TRANSFERS=1 specifies one transfer). TRANSFERS = 0 selects a different mode of operation - Skip the
                            number of items defined by ITEMS, then generate one item without updating the state of the address
                            generator. This mode is used for applying error correction to the Outer Decoder input data. When
                            TRANSFERSMODE=1: ITEMS[23:0] (TRANSFERS is internally fixed at 1). Note: when EOPMODE = '10',
                            TRANSFERS > 1 is not supported. */

