/* WLANMIMODECODEROFDMSYMBOLS @Bits 0..9 : Specify the number of OFDM symbols for which the channel matrices are valid. Once the
                                           specified number of OFDM symbols have been processed, the channel matrices are
                                           invalidated, and a new set of channel matrices will be used. Provided suitable
                                           hardware support is enabled, it is possible to pre-load the next set of channel
                                           matrices whilst processing receive vectors with the current set of channel matrices.
                                           Note that once the current set of channel matrices have been invalidated, no new
                                           receive vectors will be processed until the next set of channel matrices have been
                                           loaded (or pre-loaded). When this register is set to zero, the channel matrices will
                                           never be invalidated, and subsequent channel matrix loads will overwrite existing
                                           data in-place. */

